This script is a well-structured resume parser using PyMuPDF (fitz) and regex, customized to extract structured data like name, phone number, email, region, education, and graduation year from PDF resumes stored in a folder.

✅ Here's what the script does well:
Extracts names from filenames while stripping common resume terms (like "cv", "2023", "jan", etc.).

Searches for phone numbers, emails, education levels, and graduation years using regex.

Filters regions based on a predefined list of Bahraini cities.

Returns a clean Pandas DataFrame and saves it to Excel.

